        "VOCAB|||Negotiation Terms|||Enhance your vocabulary with these essential terms and natural expressions:\n\n*   **Leverage** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **A dealbreaker** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **To compromise** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **Bottom line** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **To meet halfway.** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n\n> 🗣️ **Pronunciation Tip:** Keep your vowels clean and practice saying these terms slowly.|||Elo: A 'dealbreaker' is an absolute 'no'. What's a dealbreaker for you in a job offer?",
        "CONCEPT|||Anchoring and Silence|||The first number said is the 'anchor'. Once you state your terms, be completely silent. Let them fill the silence.\n\n*   **Key Concept Explanation:** Understanding this rule allows you to sound natural and confident when speaking.\n*   **How it works:** Apply this structure directly in daily conversations.\n\n> 💡 **Tutor Pro-Tip:** Don't translate directly from Portuguese! Focus on the English chunk structure.|||Elo: Silence is powerful. Americans hate silence and will often negotiate against themselves to fill it.",
