        "VOCAB|||Crisis Terms|||Enhance your vocabulary with these essential terms and natural expressions:\n\n*   **To mitigate** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **Damage control** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **A PR nightmare** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **To take full responsibility** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n*   **A contingency plan.** - Learn to use this in a complete sentence.\n\n> 🗣️ **Pronunciation Tip:** Keep your vowels clean and practice saying these terms slowly.|||Elo: 'We need a contingency plan' = Plan B.",
        "CONCEPT|||The Non-Apology Apology|||Beware of saying 'I'm sorry you feel that way'. It shifts the blame. A real apology takes ownership: 'I apologize for the oversight.'\n\n*   **Key Concept Explanation:** Understanding this rule allows you to sound natural and confident when speaking.\n*   **How it works:** Apply this structure directly in daily conversations.\n\n> 💡 **Tutor Pro-Tip:** Don't translate directly from Portuguese! Focus on the English chunk structure.|||Elo: Ownership builds trust, even when you mess up.",
